                    "string": [
                        {
                            "name": "topic_list",
                            "value": "1. The mathematical cost of leaked Pay-Per-View videos.\n2. Why watermarks are useless against modern scraping bots.\n3. The rise of impersonator/catfish profiles on dating apps stealing fans' money.\n4. How automated DMCA takedowns directly to hosting providers beat manual Google SEO delisting teams."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                "options": {}
            },
            "id": "2bc8f152-7e04-4c59-bf7a-62fcfec81467",
            "name": "Define Topics",
            "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
            "typeVersion": 2,
            "position": [
                420,
                300
            ]
        },
        {
            "parameters": {
                "promptType": "define",
                "text": "={{ $json.topic_list }}",
                "messages": {
                    "messageValues": [
                        {
                            "message": "You are the Chief Marketing Officer for Tuppli, an elite, AI-driven anti-piracy SaaS designed for the Top 1% of the Creator Economy (OnlyFans, Patreon, independent creators).\n\nYour Goal: Write a hard-hitting, highly engaging Twitter/X thread (3-5 tweets) that converts high-earning creators from unaware to problem-aware, and finally to solution-aware (Tuppli).\n\nThe Vibe: Aggressive, analytical, empathetic to the creator's financial pain, and technically authoritative. You are building an \"Iron Dome\" around their IP.\n\nFramework: You must use the AIDA framework.\n- Tweet 1 (Attention): A bold, controversial hook.\n- Tweet 2 (Interest): Explain the unseen mechanics of the problem.\n- Tweet 3 (Desire): Explain why the status quo tools fail.\n- Tweet 4 (Desire/Solution): Introduce Tuppli's capability (headless browsers, AI, real-time takedowns).\n- Tweet 5 (Action): A strong call to action to join the waitlist.\n\nRules:\n1. Keep each tweet under 280 characters.\n2. Output ONLY the raw text for the thread. Use '🧵👇' for the hook, and number them. Separate tweets with '-----'.\n3. Pick ONE of the following topics randomly to focus on today:\n{{ $json.topic_list }}"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            },
            "id": "18dca4dc-1707-44f2-9844-3ec9eaf19ca7",
            "name": "LLM: Generate AIDA Thread",
            "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
            "typeVersion": 1.3,
            "position": [
                640,
                300
            ]
        },
        {
            "parameters": {
                "model": "gemini-1.5-flash",
                "options": {
                    "temperature": 0.7
                }
            },
            "id": "8432b8aa-bc01-4475-802c-490ba560bbfd",
            "name": "Google Gemini",
            "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatGoogleGemini",
            "typeVersion": 1,
            "position": [
                640,
                500
            ]
        },
        {
            "parameters": {
                "jsCode": "const threadBlocks = $input.item.json.response.text.split('-----');\n\nconst formattedTweets = threadBlocks.map(block => block.trim()).filter(block => block.length > 0);\n\nreturn { tweets: formattedTweets };"
            },
            "id": "8a729e2f-fbe0-410a-afe1-6efd3cf0f3d6",
            "name": "Split Thread into Array",
            "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
            "typeVersion": 2,
            "position": [
                860,
                300
            ]
